blocks.body:
For A (m × n) and B (n × p):
    rank(A) + rank(B) − n ≤ rank(AB) ≤ min{rank(A), rank(B)}
The n subtracted is the SHARED dimension — the number of columns of A, equal to the rows of B. Getting that wrong is the commonest error in applying it.

solution.math:
rank(AB) ≥ rank(A) + rank(B) − n = 3 + 3 − 5 = 1
attained: A = diag(1,1,1,0,0), B with image span{e₁, e₄, e₅}
then rank(AB) = 1 ✓
